========================================================
DEVOPS NOTEBOOK — .dockerignore
========================================================

.dockerignore tells Docker what NOT to send as build
context when building an image.

Common examples:

node_modules
.git
.env
coverage

WHY?

1. Smaller build context
2. Faster builds
3. Avoid unnecessary files
4. Avoid accidentally including local secrets

IMPORTANT:

.gitignore and .dockerignore have different purposes.

.gitignore
    ↓
Controls what Git tracks.

.dockerignore
    ↓
Controls what Docker receives during build.

========================================================*/